{
  "meta": {
    "document": "City of Richmond VA FY2027 Adopted Budget",
    "title": "Richmond — the money trail",
    "grand_total": 3485014795,
    "year": 2027,
    "note": "Richmond is an independent city — it belongs to no county and does both city and county jobs itself. This is the adopted all-funds budget for FY2027, $3.49 billion; the General Fund (the main operating budget) is $1.10 billion. One honest caveat the city’s own book carries: the $3.49B is a gross figure that counts internal transfers twice — the $257M the General Fund sends to the schools also appears inside the schools’ own $581M fund — so netting those out, real spending is about $3.13 billion. Richmond is unusual in owning a municipal natural-gas utility. Every figure ties to the adopted budget book and foots to the dollar."
  },
